From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elena Maher <12779416+elenaOnline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 21:02:18 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gpui: Draw the shadows between a run's meshes inside the run
 (Metal)

The Metal renderer rasterizes a run of mesh batches, and the sprites painted
between them, in one pass through the multisampled path texture. A shadow
batch ended the run, so a canvas whose cards cast drop shadows (sticky notes)
drew every visible card in a pass of its own: a render encoder for the
full-window 4x MSAA texture, a clear and resolve, a composite and the main
pass reopened. With 400 notes on screen, encoding a frame took ~40 ms.

Shadows painted between a run's meshes are now drawn inside the run, in
order, with a shadow pipeline for the multisampled path texture (the sprite
blending that stores premultiplied colour), and the run's composite covers
their painted area (shadow_bounds). mesh_run_end (gpui::scene) is the one
definition of a run; Scene::mesh_passes and the test-support
Window::mesh_passes count the passes a frame's meshes take.

The headless benchmark path (render_scene) also stops making new path
textures for every frame it renders: only for a new size, as a window does
on resize.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
